#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/4
msgid ""
"The other one is Maderas.\n"
msgstr ""
"另一座是马德拉斯。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/5
msgid ""
"It's never erupted in recorded history. There's a\n"
"lake in the caldera at the top.\n"
msgstr ""
"有历史记录以来它从未喷发过。山顶的\n"
"火山口里有一个湖。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/6
msgid ""
"A crater lake... Let's hope there's not another\n"
"underground factory inside...\n"
msgstr ""
"火山口湖……希望里面没有另一个\n"
"地下工厂……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/7
msgid ""
"Don't say that!\n"
msgstr ""
"别这么说！\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/8
msgid ""
"If Peace Walker's nukes detonated there, it would\n"
"destabilize the magma underneath.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果和平行者号的核弹在那里引爆，会\n"
"破坏下方岩浆的稳定。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/9
msgid ""
"It could cause the volcano to erupt again.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能导致火山再次喷发。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/10
msgid ""
"If that happens, my country is doomed. Snake, you\n"
"must stop Peace Walker!\n"
msgstr ""
"那样我国就完了。斯内克，你\n"
"必须阻止和平行者！\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/0
msgid ""
"We are Sandinistas, the heirs of General Sandino's\n"
"will.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是桑地诺人，继承桑地诺将军\n"
"遗志。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/1
msgid ""
"Sandino... the father of modern guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺……现代游击战之父。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/2
msgid ""
"To you, maybe. To us, he's more like a real father.\n"
msgstr ""
"对你或许。对我们，他更像真父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/3
msgid ""
"That why you named yourselves after him?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你们以他命名？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/4
msgid ""
"Of course. La Frente Sandinista de Liberación\n"
"Nacional...\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。桑地诺民族解放\n"
"阵线……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/5
msgid ""
"the Sandinista National Liberation Front is named\n"
"in his honor.\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺民族解放阵线以\n"
"他命名，以示纪念。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/6
msgid ""
"We share the General's goal - to take back our\n"
"country's freedom.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们和将军目标一致，夺回我们\n"
"国家的自由。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/7
msgid ""
"In his day, from America. In ours, from the despot\n"
"Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"他那时，敌人来自美国。我们这时，敌人是暴君\n"
"索摩查。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/8
msgid ""
"Times have changed, but the song remains the\n"
"same.\n"
msgstr ""
"时代变了，但歌还是那首\n"
"歌。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/9
msgid ""
"\"Patria Libre o Morir\"... That is our slogan.\n"
msgstr ""
"“自由祖国或死亡”……这是我们的口号。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/10
msgid ""
"El Che used to say the same thing, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"切也曾说过同样的话。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/11
msgid ""
"\"Patria o Muerte\"... the slogan of the Cuban\n"
"Revolution.\n"
msgstr ""
"“祖国或死亡”……古巴\n"
"革命的标语。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/12
msgid ""
"So you're fighting for a socialist revolution, too,\n"
"then?\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说你们也是在为社会主义革命而战，\n"
"是吗？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/13
msgid ""
"No. It's not about ideology. We only want to live\n"
"normal lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"不。无关意识形态。我们只想\n"
"正常生活。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/14
msgid ""
"We are sick of living in a country where you can\n"
"be beaten for walking down the street.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们受够了生活在一个可能因为走在街上\n"
"就被殴打的国家。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/15
msgid ""
"Where you never know if your neighbor is snitching\n"
"on you.\n"
msgstr ""
"在那儿，你不知邻居会不会背后\n"
"告发你。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/16
msgid ""
"Our goal is to give back the country to its people.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们的目标是把国家还给人民。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/17
msgid ""
"Yeah. The Cuban Revolution started out like that,\n"
"too...\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。古巴革命当初也这样开始，\n"
"也是……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/18
msgid ""
"We are few in number, but we will win.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们人少，但会赢。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/19
msgid ""
"Victoria o muerte. For a revolutionary, there is no\n"
"other fate.\n"
msgstr ""
"胜利或死亡。对革命者来说，没有\n"
"别的命运。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/0
msgid ""
"Augusto César Sandino... general and hero of\n"
"Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"奥古斯托·塞萨尔·桑地诺……尼加拉瓜的\n"
"将军和英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/1
msgid ""
"Fifty years ago, conflict broke out between the\n"
"political parties of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"五十年前，尼加拉瓜各政党之间\n"
"爆发了冲突。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/2
msgid ""
"The U.S. Marines intervened in the name of\n"
"restoring order.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国海军陆战队以恢复秩序为名\n"
"干预。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/3
msgid ""
"The only one who refused to listen to their call for\n"
"reconciliation was General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"唯一拒绝响应他们和解呼吁的人，\n"
"就是桑地诺将军。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/4
msgid ""
"One man against the Marines... That takes guts.\n"
msgstr ""
"一人对抗海军陆战队……真有种。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/5
msgid ""
"The General wasn't a professional soldier. Neither\n"
"were his compadres.\n"
msgstr ""
"将军不是职业军人。他的\n"
"兄弟们也不是。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/6
msgid ""
"And they certainly could not match the Marines'\n"
"equipment.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们当然无法匹敌海军陆战队的\n"
"装备。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/7
msgid ""
"But he used the land to his advantage, lurking in\n"
"the fields and hills of Nicaragua,\n"
msgstr ""
"但他利用地形优势，潜伏在\n"
"尼加拉瓜的田野和山丘之中，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/8
msgid ""
"and using surprise attacks to harass the Marines.\n"
msgstr ""
"用突袭骚扰海军陆战队。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/9
msgid ""
"I know. I've read plenty of textbooks on guerrilla\n"
"warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。我读过不少关于游击战的\n"
"教科书。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/10
msgid ""
"In the end, he drove them out. He was truly a role\n"
"model for us.\n"
msgstr ""
"最终，他赶走了他们。他真是我们的\n"
"榜样。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, but that was the '30s - didn't the Depression\n"
"have something to do with it?\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，但那是30年代——大萧条\n"
"跟这没关系吗？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/12
msgid ""
"It takes cash to wage war.\n"
msgstr ""
"打仗得花钱。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/13
msgid ""
"Perhaps. But there is no denying what the General\n"
"accomplished.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许吧。但将军的成就\n"
"无可否认。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/14
msgid ""
"The people hailed him as the \"General de Hombres\n"
"Libres\" - the general of free men.\n"
msgstr ""
"人民称他为“自由人将军”\n"
"——General de Hombres Libres。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/15
msgid ""
"They loved him. And then...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们爱戴他。然后……\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/16
msgid ""
"He was assassinated - by Anastasio Somoza\n"
"Garcia, commander of la Guardia.\n"
msgstr ""
"他被暗杀了——凶手是安纳斯塔西奥·索摩查·\n"
"加西亚，国民警卫队司令。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/17
msgid ""
"The father of the current Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"现任索摩查的父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/18
msgid ""
"Somoza had the Americans' backing. That is the\n"
"way things were.\n"
msgstr ""
"索摩查有美国人的支持。事情\n"
"就是这样。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/19
msgid ""
"The General may be dead, and the times may have\n"
"changed,\n"
msgstr ""
"将军可能已经死了，时代可能已经\n"
"变了，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/20
msgid ""
"but his will lives on inside each of us.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他意志活在我们每人心中。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/21
msgid ""
"We are the sons and daughters of General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是桑地诺将军的儿女。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/0
msgid ""
"Hey. How's the watermelon business these days?\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，最近西瓜生意怎么样？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/1
msgid ""
"Not bad. I hear the compas back home are hanging\n"
"in there, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"不错。我听说家乡的同志们也\n"
"在坚持。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 1797..2117
#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/2
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/2
msgid ""
"Good to hear.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就好。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/3
msgid ""
"...You know our nickname. I'm impressed.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你竟知我们绰号，佩服。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/4
msgid ""
"No wonder they call you Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"难怪人家叫你BOSS。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/5
msgid ""
"You used to hide your weapons in hollowed-out\n"
"watermelons,\n"
msgstr ""
"你们以前把武器藏在挖空的\n"
"西瓜里，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/6
msgid ""
"smuggle 'em right past the National Guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"就这么混过国民警卫队。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/7
msgid ""
"You even transported pineapple grenades that\n"
"way.\n"
msgstr ""
"你们甚至那样\n"
"运菠萝手榴弹。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/8
msgid ""
"The name caught on among sympathizers in the\n"
"region and...\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字在地区同情者中\n"
"传开，而且……\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/9
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/39
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/18
msgid ""
"What are you talking about?\n"
msgstr ""
"你在说什么？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/11
msgid ""
"They call us watermelon sellers because the\n"
"General's name\n"
msgstr ""
"他们叫我们西瓜贩子，因为\n"
"将军的名字\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/12
msgid ""
"sounds like the word for watermelon, sandía.\n"
msgstr ""
"听起来像西瓜，sandía。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/13
#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/9
msgid ""
"...Really?\n"
msgstr ""
"…真？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/14
msgid ""
"Si.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/15
msgid ""
"Dammit, Kaz...\n"
msgstr ""
"可恶，卡兹…\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/0
msgid ""
"A revolution to bring peace to your country, huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"为祖国带来和平的革命，是吗。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/1
msgid ""
"No matter how much we fight, peace never gets\n"
"any closer, does it?\n"
msgstr ""
"无论怎么战斗，\n"
"和平都没有更近一步。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/2
msgid ""
"I do not like it, but it is the only way.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也不喜欢，但别无他法。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/3
msgid ""
"If we do not fight back, they'll just keep exploiting\n"
"us.\n"
msgstr ""
"不反抗，他们就\n"
"会一直压榨我们。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/4
msgid ""
"You want proof? Look at our country's history.\n"
msgstr ""
"要证据？看看我国的历史。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/5
msgid ""
"Revolution is a means and not an end, I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道，革命是手段而非目的。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/6
msgid ""
"When the revolution is victorious, I want my\n"
"country to be at peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"革命胜利后，\n"
"我希望祖国能享有和平。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/7
msgid ""
"But to bring peace, we have to first eliminate that\n"
"traitorous scum.\n"
msgstr ""
"但要实现和平，\n"
"就得先除掉那个叛徒败类。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/8
msgid ""
"It's an old saying: \"We make war that we may live\n"
"in peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"有句老话：「我们发动战争，\n"
"是为了能生活在和平中。」\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/9
msgid ""
"Who said it?\n"
msgstr ""
"谁说的？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/10
msgid ""
"Aristotle.\n"
msgstr ""
"亚里士多德。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/11
msgid ""
"You know your history.\n"
msgstr ""
"你很懂历史。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/12
msgid ""
"I had a good teacher.\n"
msgstr ""
"我有个好老师。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/13
msgid ""
"It has always been like this.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/14
msgid ""
"People making the same mistakes, over and over...\n"
"and still all we can do is fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3d40/15
msgid ""
"I hear ya. If you've got a goal, you've got to keep\n"
"moving forward.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/0
msgid ""
"I noticed you call Che Guevara \"El Che.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"你管切·格瓦拉叫“El Che”。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/1
msgid ""
"Not just us. Everyone in these parts does.\n"
msgstr ""
"不只我们。这的人都这么叫。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/2
msgid ""
"\"Che\" was always his nickname. It does not feel\n"
"right to call him by his last name.\n"
msgstr ""
"“切”一直是他的昵称。叫他\n"
"姓，感觉不对。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/3
msgid ""
"...I was shocked the first time I saw you. You look\n"
"so much like him.\n"
msgstr ""
"…我第一次见你时很震惊。你太像\n"
"他了。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/4
msgid ""
"I look like \"El Che\", huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"我像“El Che”？\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/5
msgid ""
"Sort of. Not in the face. It's more... the way you\n"
"carry yourself...\n"
msgstr ""
"有点像。不是脸。更像是…你的\n"
"举手投足…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 7397..8136
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/6
msgid ""
"I guess Che's a hero to the Sandinistas, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"切对桑地诺派来说也是英雄吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 8164..10156
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/7
msgid ""
"Of course. The FSLN was formed in the spirit of\n"
"the ideologies championed by El Che and Fidel.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。FSLN正是本着El Che和\n"
"菲德尔所倡导的思想成立的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 10421..12775
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/8
msgid ""
"Fidel... Fidel Castro. So you're trying to bring the\n"
"Cuban Revolution to Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"菲德尔…卡斯特罗。你们想把\n"
"古巴革命带到尼加拉瓜。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 12845..14642
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/9
msgid ""
"Well, we were. But Cuba isn't what it once was...\n"
"Not since El Che left.\n"
msgstr ""
"曾经是。但古巴已不复当年…\n"
"自El Che走后。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 14740..16314
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/10
msgid ""
"El Che was a true revolutionary. He fought - and\n"
"died - for the people.\n"
msgstr ""
"El Che是真正的革命者。他为人民\n"
"战斗——并牺牲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 16370..17387
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/11
msgid ""
"He worked harder than anybody, and he was a\n"
"righteous man.\n"
msgstr ""
"他比谁都努力，他是个\n"
"正直的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 17442..19045
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/12
msgid ""
"Even as a minister of Cuba, he gave up his\n"
"weekends to work on the farms and public works.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使身为古巴部长，他也放弃周末\n"
"去农场和公共工程干活。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19100..19560
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/13
msgid ""
"As a volunteer, no less.\n"
msgstr ""
"还是当志愿者。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19644..20271
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/14
msgid ""
"Yeah, I've heard the stories.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，故事我听过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 20326..21441
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/15
msgid ""
"But when you think about it, wasn't it that\n"
"obsession that did him in?\n"
msgstr ""
"但想想看，不正是那份\n"
"执念害了他吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21483..21831
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 2048..2326
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/16
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/1
msgid ""
"How do you mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21887..23517
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/17
msgid ""
"We can't all be supermen. He thought the ideals he\n"
"applied in Cuba would work in Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不可能都是超人。他以为古巴\n"
"行得通的理想，玻利维亚也行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 23558..25077
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/18
msgid ""
"But, he failed to win converts and the support of\n"
"the peasants, and it cost him his life.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他没能争取到皈依者和\n"
"农民的支持，为此丢了命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 25175..25927
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/19
msgid ""
"Maybe... maybe you're right.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许…你说得对。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 26010..27278
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/20
msgid ""
"But at least he did not steal from those peasants,\n"
"no matter how hard things got.\n"
msgstr ""
"但至少他没偷农民的东西，\n"
"再难也没偷。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 27320..27473
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0080_000_0
#. timeline 24478..24840
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 2507..2702
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 1309..1476
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/21
#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/14
#: codec/1/206/0xce040/7
#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/2
#: codec/1/235/0xebf60/23
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/2
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/1
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/12
#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/1
msgid ""
"Yeah.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 27515..28017
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/22
msgid ""
"I can sympathize with that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我能理解。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 28100..29312
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/23
msgid ""
"There's plenty of guerrillas out there who'd rob\n"
"their own people to feed their revolutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"游击队里多的是抢自己人\n"
"喂革命的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 29354..31249
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/24
msgid ""
"If we had a comandante like him, the Sandinistas\n"
"would find the will to fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"若有个像他的指挥官，桑地诺\n"
"就有斗志了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 501..1407
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/0
msgid ""
"You called that giant chopper an \"hombre nuevo\"...\n"
msgstr ""
"你把那架大直升机叫\"hombre nuevo\"……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 1407..2201
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/1
msgid ""
"Si. It means \"new man.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Si，意为\"新人\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 2229..2563
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/2
msgid ""
"\"New man\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"\"新人\"？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 2605..3789
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/3
msgid ""
"There was nobody piloting that thing. It must be\n"
"controlled by machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"那东西根本没人驾驶。肯定是由机器\n"
"控制的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 3817..5391
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/4
msgid ""
"Yeah, it seems that way. No human being could pull\n"
"off those crazy maneuvers.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，看来如此。没人能做出\n"
"那些疯狂动作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 5433..6561
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/5
msgid ""
"But it's not crazy - it's smart. It sings, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"那不叫疯，叫聪明。它还会唱歌。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 6603..8038
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/6
msgid ""
"When we first saw it, one of my men said, \"Pilot\n"
"must be an hombre nuevo.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"初见时，我手下说：“飞行员\n"
"准是新人。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 8080..8721
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/7
msgid ""
"Me, I do not like the name.\n"
msgstr ""
"我嘛，不喜欢这名字。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 8735..8986
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/8
#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/2
msgid ""
"Why?\n"
msgstr ""
"为什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 9000..10017
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/9
msgid ""
"\"Hombre nuevo\" was what El Che was striving to\n"
"become.\n"
msgstr ""
"“新人”正是切·格瓦拉想\n"
"成为的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 10058..11326
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/10
msgid ""
"What all of us who joined the Sandinistas strive to\n"
"become. That's why!\n"
msgstr ""
"我们加入桑地诺的人都想\n"
"成为那样。就是这样！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 11368..12789
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/11
msgid ""
"An hombre nuevo is one who finds joy in virtue\n"
"and voluntary labor...\n"
msgstr ""
"新人就是在美德\n"
"和自愿劳动中找到快乐的人……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 12845..13931
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/12
msgid ""
"It makes me furious to see the name given to such\n"
"a monster.\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字用在怪物身上，\n"
"让我怒火中烧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 13973..14336
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/13
msgid ""
"I'll bet.\n"
msgstr ""
"我信。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 459..1198
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/0
msgid ""
"Chico called that helicopter el colibri...\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科管那直升机叫el colibri……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 1253..2229
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/1
msgid ""
"Our name for the hummingbird. You saw how that\n"
"chopper moved...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们给蜂鸟起的名字。你看到那架\n"
"直升机是怎么动的了……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 2270..2856
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/2
msgid ""
"how it hovered in midair like a hummingbird.\n"
msgstr ""
"像蜂鸟一样悬停在空中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 2911..3650
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/3
msgid ""
"Hell've a lot bigger than a bird, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"可它比鸟大太多了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 3691..4500
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/4
msgid ""
"True. But better than hombre nuevo, don't you\n"
"think?\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。但比“新人”更好，你不\n"
"觉得吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 4555..5419
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/5
msgid ""
"When you get kidnapped by el colibri, it's all over.\n"
msgstr ""
"被el colibri抓走，就完了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 5503..6673
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/6
msgid ""
"They take you to a prison camp, and torture you\n"
"until you snitch on your compas.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会把你带到战俘营，折磨你\n"
"直到你出卖你的战友。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 6715..7202
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/7
msgid ""
"That's what took Chico...\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科就是这么被抓的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 7244..8484
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/8
msgid ""
"They have no mercy. Once you've talked, they toss\n"
"you out like trash...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们毫不留情。你一开口，\n"
"就被当垃圾扔掉……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 8582..9459
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/9
msgid ""
"I knew this, and still I could not save Chico.\n"
msgstr ""
"我明知如此，却还是救不了奇科。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 9613..10616
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/10
msgid ""
"If he cannot be saved, I'll do what must be done...\n"
msgstr ""
"如果救不了他，我会做该做的事……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 10671..11187
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/11
msgid ""
"Don't write him off like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"别这么早就放弃他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 11270..12538
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/12
msgid ""
"Sometimes you have to survive, even if it means\n"
"sacrificing your honor.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时你必须活下去，即使这意味着\n"
"牺牲你的荣誉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 12594..13486
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/13
msgid ""
"I'll get him back. I promise.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会把他带回来。我保证。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/0
msgid ""
"Snake, I need your opinion. How strong are the\n"
"enemy's mercenaries?\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，我需要你的看法。敌人的雇佣兵\n"
"有多强？\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/1
msgid ""
"They're well trained. They've got more than enough\n"
"men...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们训练有素，人手\n"
"绰绰有余……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/2
msgid ""
"Seasoned, too - a lot of them probably saw action\n"
"in Vietnam. They're a tough bunch.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且老练，很多人可能在越南\n"
"打过仗。他们很难缠。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/3
msgid ""
"And armed to the teeth.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且全副武装。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/4
msgid ""
"I don't think I've ever seen a mercenary force field\n"
"that many tanks and attack choppers.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想我从没见过一支雇佣兵部队能部署\n"
"那么多坦克和攻击直升机。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/5
msgid ""
"It shows how much cash they have to throw\n"
"around.\n"
msgstr ""
"说明他们有多少钱可以随意\n"
"挥霍。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/6
msgid ""
"And connections - how did they get access to\n"
"such weapons?\n"
msgstr ""
"还有人脉，他们怎么弄到\n"
"这种武器的？\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/7
msgid ""
"How do you think? They're backed by the one and\n"
"only CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"你说呢？背后正是\n"
"独一无二的CIA。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/8
msgid ""
"And here we are, half of us farmers and the other\n"
"half students. Children, even!\n"
msgstr ""
"而我们呢，一半是农民，另一半\n"
"是学生。甚至还有孩子！\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/9
msgid ""
"And weapons... We're so short on guns we have to\n"
"steal them from the enemy.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有武器……我们枪太少了，只能\n"
"从敌人那里偷。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/10
msgid ""
"As much as I hate to say it, we're always going to\n"
"be on the defensive.\n"
msgstr ""
"尽管我很不想这么说，但我们永远都会\n"
"处于守势。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/12
msgid ""
"And mi viejo... Without him, we...\n"
msgstr ""
"还有我老爹……没了他，我们……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 16258..16690
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/13
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/15
msgid ""
"Yeah, I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，我知道。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/14
msgid ""
"...I don't know if we can win.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不知能不能赢。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/15
msgid ""
"Can we, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"我们能赢吗，SNAKE？\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/16
msgid ""
"Stop feeling sorry for yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"别自怨自艾了。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/17
#: codec/2/905/0x389770/4
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/48
msgid ""
"But...\n"
msgstr ""
"可是……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/18
msgid ""
"Amanda!\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 4959..5099
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3761..3914
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_myo_rad_0190_000_0
#. timeline 417..557
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/19
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/3
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/3
#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/17
#: codec/1/255/0xff000/8
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/21
#: codec/2/904/0x388570/13
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/46
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/12
#: codec/2/916/0x394f90/4
#: codec/2/916/0x394f90/13
#: codec/2/919/0x3971e0/1
msgid ""
"What?\n"
msgstr ""
"啥\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/20
msgid ""
"Listen to me. Don't ever let your men hear you talk\n"
"like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"听我说。别让手下听见你\n"
"说这种话。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/21
msgid ""
"...I...\n"
msgstr ""
"……我……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/22
msgid ""
"You're their leader, and a leader has to stand tall.\n"
"Even when times get tough.\n"
msgstr ""
"你是他们的领袖，领袖必须挺直腰杆。\n"
"哪怕时局艰难。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/23
msgid ""
"When it feels like the fear and uncertainty could\n"
"crush you.\n"
msgstr ""
"当恐惧和不安仿佛\n"
"要把你压垮时。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/24
msgid ""
"You're the one your comrades look to for\n"
"reassurance. That's what a leader is. Don't forget it.\n"
msgstr ""
"战友们指望你来安心。\n"
"这就是领袖。别忘了。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/25
msgid ""
"...Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"……SNAKE……\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/26
msgid ""
"If you're looking for comfort, go find a church.\n"
"That's all I've got to say.\n"
msgstr ""
"想找安慰，去教堂。\n"
"我就说这些。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/27
msgid ""
"You are right. I am sorry. I need to pull myself\n"
"together.\n"
msgstr ""
"你说得对。抱歉。我得\n"
"振作起来。\n"

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/28
msgid ""
"You'll be fine. I know you have it in you.\n"
msgstr ""
"你会没事，你有这本事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/0
msgid ""
"Claymores are directional anti-personnel landmines.\n"
msgstr ""
"阔刀地雷是定向杀伤人员地雷。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 1448..2382
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/1
msgid ""
"Their blast radius is approximately 70 vara (60 yd),\n"
msgstr ""
"杀伤半径约70瓦拉（60码），\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 2396..3900
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/2
msgid ""
"sending over 700 metal fragments through the air\n"
"at a 60º angle.\n"
msgstr ""
"以60度角抛射出\n"
"700多枚金属破片。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 3928..5252
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/3
msgid ""
"But since they're directional, you can simply disarm\n"
"them from their blind side.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过因为它是定向的，\n"
"从背面就能直接拆除。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 5280..6854
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/4
msgid ""
"Get down low and approach the mine from behind,\n"
"then deactivate and recover it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 6882..7941
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/5
msgid ""
"To do this, press <I=ACT> when the Icon appears.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 7955..8805
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/6
msgid ""
"You can use any unused Claymores you recover.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 8832..9543
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/7
msgid ""
"You can also destroy them by shooting them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 9571..11034
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/8
msgid ""
"Just keep your distance or you'll get hit by\n"
"shrapnel. Best to use a sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0230_000_0
#. timeline 11061..12190
#: codec/1/197/0xc5eb0/9
msgid ""
"The only downside is you can forget about using\n"
"them yourself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/0
msgid ""
"The land in our country belongs to us, and yet it\n"
"doesn't belong to us.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们国家的土地属于我们，\n"
"却又不属于我们。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/2
msgid ""
"Along the coast, it is all banana groves. And in the\n"
"mountains, it is coffee.\n"
msgstr ""
"沿海全是香蕉园。山里\n"
"则是咖啡。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/3
msgid ""
"I guess in that way it's not so different from here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说来跟这里也差不多。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/4
msgid ""
"Plantations...\n"
msgstr ""
"庄园……\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/5
msgid ""
"Almost all the bananas and coffee are sold as\n"
"exports.\n"
msgstr ""
"几乎全部香蕉和咖啡都\n"
"出口卖掉。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/6
msgid ""
"The landlords keep the money for themselves,\n"
"leaving precious little to the farmers.\n"
msgstr ""
"地主把钱据为己有，\n"
"只留给农民一丁点。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/7
msgid ""
"Worse, the biggest landowners in the country are\n"
"Somoza and his family.\n"
msgstr ""
"更糟的是，全国最大的地主\n"
"就是索摩查一家。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/8
msgid ""
"But it does bring in foreign currency...\n"
msgstr ""
"但至少能赚外汇……\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/9
msgid ""
"I doubt even that, at least for bananas. The\n"
"plantations are owned by American corporations.\n"
msgstr ""
"我看未必，至少香蕉不是。\n"
"种植园属于美国公司。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/10
msgid ""
"The bananas are processed in factories on the\n"
"plantations and exported to America from private\n"
"ports...\n"
msgstr ""
"香蕉在种植园里的工厂加工，\n"
"然后从私人港口出口到美国……\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/11
msgid ""
"It's like having little American enclaves along the\n"
"coast of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像尼加拉瓜沿海\n"
"散布着美国飞地。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/12
msgid ""
"But the farmers have no choice but to go work\n"
"there...\n"
msgstr ""
"可农民别无选择，只能\n"
"去那里干活……\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/13
msgid ""
"Es ridículo! The people have to take their land\n"
"back.\n"
msgstr ""
"太荒唐了！人民必须\n"
"夺回土地。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/14
msgid ""
"It is one of the things we're fighting for.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是我们战斗的目标之一。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/0
msgid ""
"Tell me... when exactly did you realize your dad\n"
"was working with the KGB?\n"
msgstr ""
"告诉我……你究竟何时\n"
"发现你父亲在为克格勃做事？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/1
msgid ""
"About six months ago. Up until then, we only had\n"
"beans to eat.\n"
msgstr ""
"大约半年前。在那之前，\n"
"我们只有豆子吃。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/2
msgid ""
"And then suddenly we started to get eggs and\n"
"flour. Our bullet shortage simply disappeared.\n"
msgstr ""
"后来突然有了蛋和面粉。\n"
"子弹短缺就这么没了。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/3
msgid ""
"How'd he get the cocaine?\n"
msgstr ""
"可卡因哪来的？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/4
msgid ""
"Ask the KGB. All we did here was process it.\n"
msgstr ""
"问克格勃。我们只管加工。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/5
msgid ""
"Coca plants grow here, too,\n"
msgstr ""
"这里也种古柯，\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/6
msgid ""
"but to my knowledge almost all of the stuff we\n"
"used came from Colombia and Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""
"但据我所知，用的料几乎都来自\n"
"哥伦比亚和玻利维亚。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/7
msgid ""
"It's processed in a factory and then shipped to\n"
"ports on the Caribbean Sea.\n"
msgstr ""
"在工厂加工后运往\n"
"加勒比海沿岸港口。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/8
msgid ""
"Where does it go after that?\n"
msgstr ""
"之后运去哪？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/9
msgid ""
"I never thought about it.... I mean, I did not want to\n"
"think about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我从未想过……我是说，我不想去\n"
"想这件事。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/10
msgid ""
"The biggest cocaine consumer in the world is the\n"
"United States.\n"
msgstr ""
"全球最大的可卡因消费国就是\n"
"美国。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/11
msgid ""
"I'm guessing they smuggle it in on vessels\n"
"disguised as fishing boats.\n"
msgstr ""
"我猜是用伪装成渔船的\n"
"船走私进去。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/12
msgid ""
"Wait. La CIA uses that route, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"等等。CIA也用这条线。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/13
msgid ""
"Are you telling me they're selling cocaine to their\n"
"own country?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说他们往自己国家\n"
"卖可卡因？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/14
msgid ""
"Looks that way.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来是。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/15
msgid ""
"Those bastards are turning their own children into\n"
"junkies? Are they insane?!\n"
msgstr ""
"那帮混蛋把自家孩子变成\n"
"瘾君子？疯了吗？！\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/16
msgid ""
"No, just afraid. Afraid of a communist Central\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，只是怕。怕中美洲\n"
"落入共产党手。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/0
msgid ""
"La CIA calls their new toy Peace Walker, eh?\n"
msgstr ""
"中情局叫它和平行者？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/1
msgid ""
"Yeah... So?\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/2
msgid ""
"It is a insult to us Nicos.\n"
msgstr ""
"这对我们尼加拉瓜人是侮辱。\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/3
msgid ""
"Because of the guy you were talking about?\n"
"Walker?\n"
msgstr ""
"因为你们说的\n"
"那个人？沃克？\n"

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/4
msgid ""
"Si, although it happened over a hundred years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/5
msgid ""
"Back then, the political parties in Nicaragua were\n"
"at each other's throats.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/6
msgid ""
"The Nicaraguan Democratic Party hired an\n"
"American mercenary to help counter their enemies,\n"
"the Conservative Party.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/7
msgid ""
"And that was Walker.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/8
msgid ""
"After taking care of the Conservatives,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/9
msgid ""
"Walker decided to seize power in Nicaragua for\n"
"himself, eventually making himself president.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/10
msgid ""
"The Democratic Party gave him an inch, and he\n"
"took the whole country.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/11
msgid ""
"But it didn't end there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/12
msgid ""
"Not only did he make English an official language,\n"
"he tried to reintroduce slavery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/13
msgid ""
"Walker's goal was to build a \"Caribbean Empire\"\n"
"centered on the American South.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/14
msgid ""
"Caribbean Empire... hmh. Sounds kind of like what\n"
"Coldman is trying to pull off.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/15
msgid ""
"The gringos are always like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/16
msgid ""
"They invent some convenient excuse to trample all\n"
"over foreign countries like they own the place.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/17
msgid ""
"Peace Walker... ha!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/18
msgid ""
"What happened to Walker in the end?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/19
msgid ""
"A united Central American army led by Costa Rica\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/20
msgid ""
"kicked his ass and sent him running back to\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/21
msgid ""
"Then why don't we do the same? I for one don't\n"
"intend to let Coldman get his way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6ed0/22
msgid ""
"Good idea... I'm glad we have you, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/0
msgid ""
"Amanda! When did you join up with the Sandinistas?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达！你何时加入桑地诺派？\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/1
msgid ""
"About a year ago, when I went into the mountains\n"
"with mi viejo and his group.\n"
msgstr ""
"大概一年前，我跟老爹\n"
"和他的人进了山。\n"

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/2
msgid ""
"I thought your dad was with the FSLN from the\n"
"start.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为你爸一开始\n"
"就在FSLN。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 3719..5419
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/3
msgid ""
"No. He fought alongside General Sandino, but after\n"
"that he retired for a while.\n"
msgstr ""
"不。他跟桑地诺将军并肩作战，\n"
"之后退隐了一阵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6617
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/4
msgid ""
"He found a job, got a wife and a house, and raised\n"
"us kids.\n"
msgstr ""
"他找了工作，娶妻买房，\n"
"把我们养大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 6715..7453
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/5
msgid ""
"Then one day some Sandinista students came by...\n"
msgstr ""
"后来有天来了几个桑地诺学生……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 7481..8345
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/6
msgid ""
"And he felt the old fire in his belly?\n"
msgstr ""
"他又热血沸腾了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 8373..9654
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/7
msgid ""
"Something like that. All he did was help them\n"
"escape from la Guardia, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"差不多。不过他只是帮他们\n"
"从国民警卫队手里逃走。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 9710..10295
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/8
msgid ""
"But then la Guardia showed up.\n"
msgstr ""
"可国民警卫队来了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11549
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/9
msgid ""
"They broke into our house and began pushing him\n"
"around, shouting questions.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们闯进我家，推搡他，\n"
"吼着逼问。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12301
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/10
msgid ""
"I'm guessing he kept his mouth shut.\n"
msgstr ""
"我猜他一个字都没说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 12343..13681
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/11
msgid ""
"No matter how hard they hit him. Our house was\n"
"trashed.\n"
msgstr ""
"不管怎么打他。我们家被砸得\n"
"稀烂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 13778..14935
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/12
msgid ""
"After that, he was on their list - they harassed him\n"
"day and night.\n"
msgstr ""
"之后他上了他们的名单，日夜\n"
"骚扰他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 15032..15966
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/13
msgid ""
"It was only then that he gave himself over to the\n"
"Sandinistas.\n"
msgstr ""
"直到那时，他才投奔了\n"
"桑地诺派。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 16063..17010
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/14
msgid ""
"He kept it hidden from us at first, so we would not\n"
"get hurt.\n"
msgstr ""
"起初他瞒着我们，怕我们\n"
"受牵连。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 17387..17916
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/15
msgid ""
"He sounds like a good father.\n"
msgstr ""
"他像个好父亲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 18000..19964
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/16
msgid ""
"He was... But my mother got fed up with it. She left\n"
"us. I don't blame her.\n"
msgstr ""
"他曾是……但我妈受够了。她离开\n"
"我们。我不怪她。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 20048..20549
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/17
msgid ""
"Why didn't you go with her?\n"
msgstr ""
"你为啥不跟她走？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 20688..21329
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/18
msgid ""
"It was a hard decision, for sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"这决定确实很难。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 21455..23322
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/19
msgid ""
"But like my father, I couldn't let Somoza get away\n"
"with his crimes. But most of all...\n"
msgstr ""
"但像我父亲一样，我不能让索摩查逍遥\n"
"法外。最重要的是……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 23447..23795
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/20
#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/0
msgid ""
"Chico.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 23935..25397
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/21
msgid ""
"...He is too much like his papá. One way or the\n"
"other he was going to stay.\n"
msgstr ""
"……他太像他爸了。无论如何他都\n"
"会留下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 25495..26080
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/22
msgid ""
"And I could not leave him behind.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不能丢下他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 26192..27459
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/23
msgid ""
"Soon enough la Guardia drove us out, and we\n"
"found ourselves in the mountains...\n"
msgstr ""
"很快国民警卫队就把我们赶了出去，我们\n"
"流落到山里……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 27599..28212
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/24
msgid ""
"It just kind of happened\n"
msgstr ""
"就这么发生了\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 28616..30009
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/25
msgid ""
"For an accidental revolutionary, you sure put up a\n"
"hell of a fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"作为一个意外的革命者，你打得可真\n"
"够狠的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 30106..31374
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/26
msgid ""
"The mountains make men into warriors. The\n"
"training is harsh,\n"
msgstr ""
"大山把人磨炼成战士。训练很\n"
"艰苦，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 31444..32531
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/27
msgid ""
"but it brings us that much closer to being hombres\n"
"nuevos.\n"
msgstr ""
"但这让我们更接近成为新\n"
"人类。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 32600..33367
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/28
msgid ""
"Chico couldn't ask for a better sister.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科再找不到更好的姐姐。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 50697..0
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/29
msgid ""
"I can see why they picked you to be comandante.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂他们为啥选你当指挥官。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/0
msgid ""
"When I was little, I came down with malaria.\n"
msgstr ""
"我小时候得过疟疾。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/1
msgid ""
"Unlucky for me, it was the bad kind. I was in a\n"
"daze the whole time,\n"
msgstr ""
"倒霉的是，是最凶的那种。我一直\n"
"昏昏沉沉，\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/2
msgid ""
"and at one point they said I was not going to make\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"有一阵他们说我挺不过\n"
"去了。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/3
msgid ""
"Malarial encephalopathy. I hear it's pretty common\n"
"in tropical malaria cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"疟疾脑病。我听说热带疟疾里挺\n"
"常见的。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/4
msgid ""
"Even today, my memory sometimes gets a little\n"
"fuzzy.\n"
msgstr ""
"到今天，我记忆有时还会有点\n"
"模糊。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/5
msgid ""
"Since then I've had this fear of mosquitoes... When\n"
"I hear them buzzing nearby, I get jumpy.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那以后我就怕蚊子……每当\n"
"听到附近嗡嗡叫，我就心惊肉跳。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/6
msgid ""
"That explains the chain-smoking?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你烟不离手？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/7
msgid ""
"Si. I thought it might help keep the mosquitoes\n"
"away, just a little.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。我以为这能赶远点蚊子，\n"
"哪怕一点点。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/8
msgid ""
"Maybe it's all in my head. You're the same way,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""
"也许是我心理作用。你也一样，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/9
msgid ""
"I will say this - I prefer a cigar over mosquitoes.\n"
msgstr ""
"我宁愿抽雪茄也不想见蚊子。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/10
msgid ""
"Me, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也是。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/11
msgid ""
"I've gotta hand it to you. It takes guts to conquer\n"
"your fear like that\n"
msgstr ""
"我服你。像那样克服\n"
"恐惧，需要很大勇气。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/12
msgid ""
"and live a guerrilla's life in the wild.\n"
msgstr ""
"在野外打游击，真需要胆量。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/13
msgid ""
"It is nothing. El Che did not let asthma stop him\n"
"from leading the revolution.\n"
msgstr ""
"这没什么。切·格瓦拉没有让哮喘阻止他\n"
"领导革命。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/14
msgid ""
"Compared to him, I am no hero.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟他比，我算不上英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/0
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to hear about your dad.\n"
msgstr ""
"你爸的事，我很遗憾。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/1
msgid ""
"Thank you for saying that... Mi viejo was the leader\n"
"of the frente.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢你这么说……我老爹曾是\n"
"frente的领袖。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/2
msgid ""
"He was the last of the generation that knew\n"
"General Sandino...\n"
msgstr ""
"他是认识桑地诺将军那代人中\n"
"最后一位……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/3
msgid ""
"He saw the General's exploits first-hand as a boy.\n"
msgstr ""
"他小时候亲眼见过将军的事迹。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/4
msgid ""
"He would tell us stories about it all the time... and\n"
"about how the General was assassinated.\n"
msgstr ""
"他总给我们讲那些故事……还有\n"
"将军是如何被暗杀的。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/5
msgid ""
"Did you know he was getting money from the KGB?\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道他从克格勃拿钱吗？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/6
msgid ""
"I had some idea... But I did not have the courage to\n"
"confront him about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我有些猜想……但我没有勇气\n"
"去当面问他。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/7
msgid ""
"I know it was a painful decision for him to make.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道那对他是个痛苦的决定。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/8
#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/9
msgid ""
"I can imagine.\n"
msgstr ""
"我能想象。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/9
msgid ""
"Yes, my father was a good man. I loved him as a\n"
"daughter. And his soldiers believed in him.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的，我父亲是好人。我像\n"
"女儿一样爱他。士兵们也信他。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/10
msgid ""
"Thanks to him, la Frente held together even in the\n"
"worst of times.\n"
msgstr ""
"多亏他，即使最艰难时，\n"
"la Frente也团结在一起。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/11
msgid ""
"I don't know if I can ever fill his shoes...\n"
msgstr ""
"不知我能否接他的班……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/0
msgid ""
"Chico's 12, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科12岁吧？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/2
msgid ""
"Isn't he a little... short for his age?\n"
msgstr ""
"他比同龄人矮了点？\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/3
msgid ""
"...Malnourishment. Food is hard to come by when\n"
"you're running around in the jungle...\n"
msgstr ""
"……营养不良。当你在丛林里\n"
"四处奔波时，食物很难弄到……\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/4
msgid ""
"He's got quite an appetite.\n"
msgstr ""
"他胃口真大。\n"

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/5
msgid ""
"I know!\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 5057..5684
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/6
msgid ""
"I didn't want him to come in the first place.\n"
msgstr ""
"我本来就不想让他来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 5726..6826
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/7
msgid ""
"But there was no one to take him in. I had no\n"
"choice but to look after him.\n"
msgstr ""
"但没人愿意收留他。我别无\n"
"选择，只能照顾他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 6882..7425
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/8
msgid ""
"Don't be so hard on yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"别太自责了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 7578..9334
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/9
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's better for a kid to be with his family\n"
"than far away, in a safe place.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时候，孩子跟家人在一起\n"
"比远在安全的地方更好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 9599..9794
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/10
msgid ""
"Thank you...\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 9905..11563
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/11
msgid ""
"Promise me this, though. When your fight is over,\n"
"make sure he gets a proper education.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过，你要答应我。等你战斗结束，\n"
"一定让他接受正规教育。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 11647..12371
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/12
msgid ""
"Give him a chance to be something other than a\n"
"guerrilla.\n"
msgstr ""
"给他机会，让他不必只做\n"
"游击队员。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 12427..13402
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/13
msgid ""
"It's not too late to teach him something other than\n"
"fighting.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在教他点战斗以外的东西\n"
"还不算晚。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 13458..14043
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/14
msgid ""
"OK. I promise.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。我答应你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 14154..14837
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/15
msgid ""
"...You know what book Chico really likes?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你知道奇科最爱什么书？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 14907..16662
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/16
msgid ""
"The \"World Encyclopedia of Mysterious Creatures.\"\n"
"The Loch Ness Monster, the Yeti...\n"
msgstr ""
"《世界神秘生物百科全书》。\n"
"尼斯湖水怪、雪人……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 16704..17526
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/17
msgid ""
"UMAs. Yeah, I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"未知生物。嗯，我知道。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 17568..18780
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/18
msgid ""
"He's still so much like a boy... I worry about him.\n"
msgstr ""
"他还像个孩子……我很担心他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 18822..20396
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/19
msgid ""
"He'll be fine. I know plenty of grown men who still\n"
"go crazy over UMAs.\n"
msgstr ""
"他会没事。我认识不少成年男人，至今\n"
"还为UMA着迷。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 20452..21260
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/20
msgid ""
"Are... are you serious?\n"
msgstr ""
"你……当真？\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/0
msgid ""
"You've taken such good care of me since you\n"
"saved me from el colibri.\n"
msgstr ""
"你从el colibri手中救了我，\n"
"一直照顾我到现在。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/1
msgid ""
"I want to return the favor.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想报答你。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/2
msgid ""
"Just wait until you're healed up. Then we'll talk.\n"
msgstr ""
"等你伤好了再说。到时候再谈。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/3
msgid ""
"I appreciate that. But you need all the help you\n"
"can get.\n"
msgstr ""
"我很感激。但你需要一切能得到的\n"
"帮助。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/4
msgid ""
"It might take a while for me to heal completely,\n"
msgstr ""
"我完全康复可能要一段时间，\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/5
msgid ""
"but I'll be fine once I'm on my feet. Put me in a\n"
"combat unit - I'll pull my weight.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我能站起来就没事。把我编入\n"
"战斗单位，我会尽本分。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/6
msgid ""
"I wouldn't expect any less from a Sandinista\n"
"comandante.\n"
msgstr ""
"对桑地诺\n"
"指挥官也不会有别的期待。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/7
msgid ""
"Enough flattery.\n"
msgstr ""
"别拍马屁。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/8
msgid ""
"But seriously, it does not feel right for me to be\n"
"sitting here while my compas are out risking their\n"
"lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"但说真的，战友们在外\n"
"拼命，我却坐在这里，\n"
"心里不是滋味。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/9
msgid ""
"One thing's for sure. Having you out in the field\n"
"would be a big boost to Sandinista morale.\n"
msgstr ""
"有一点可以肯定。有你亲临前线，\n"
"会大大鼓舞桑地诺的士气。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/10
msgid ""
"Of course, our ultimate goal is still the overthrow\n"
"of Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，我们的最终目标仍然是推翻\n"
"索摩查。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/11
msgid ""
"But until we get ourselves back in order, we will\n"
"follow your lead, wherever it takes us.\n"
msgstr ""
"但在我们重整旗鼓之前，我们会\n"
"追随你的领导，无论去向何方。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/12
msgid ""
"Glad to have you on board.\n"
msgstr ""
"很高兴你加入。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, you getting used to Mother Base?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达，在母基地还习惯吗？\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/1
msgid ""
"Yes, it is Heaven compared to living in the\n"
"mountains.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，比起山里，\n"
"这里就是天堂。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/2
msgid ""
"We're no longer constantly on the run from la\n"
"Guardia or mercenaries.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不再需要时刻躲避国民警卫队\n"
"或雇佣兵了。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/3
msgid ""
"Some of the new guys we've recruited used to be\n"
"mercenaries...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们招募的一些新人以前就是\n"
"雇佣兵……\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/4
msgid ""
"We're getting along. It was difficult at first,\n"
msgstr ""
"我们处得来。一开始挺难的，\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/5
msgid ""
"but once you talk to them you realize we've got\n"
"plenty in common.\n"
msgstr ""
"但一交谈，就会发现我们\n"
"有很多共同点。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/6
msgid ""
"I see. Good to hear.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，那就好。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/7
msgid ""
"We may be enemies, but we're all still human\n"
"beings...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们也许是敌人，但终究都是\n"
"人类……\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/8
msgid ""
"La CIA's soldiers, la Guardia... The same goes for\n"
"the people of America.\n"
msgstr ""
"中情局士兵、国民警卫队……\n"
"美国人民也一样。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/9
msgid ""
"What's gotten into you?\n"
msgstr ""
"你怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/10
msgid ""
"Mi viejo got involved with drugs in order to scrape\n"
"together money for la revolución.\n"
msgstr ""
"我老爸为了给革命凑钱，\n"
"卷入了毒品交易。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/11
msgid ""
"He did whatever the KGB said.\n"
msgstr ""
"克格勃让他干什么他就干什么。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/12
msgid ""
"All for Nicaragua... or so he told himself.\n"
msgstr ""
"全为尼加拉瓜，他这么想。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/13
msgid ""
"But I realize now... In the end all he did was help\n"
"poison young people of America.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我现在明白……到头来他只是帮\n"
"毒害美国年轻人。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/15
msgid ""
"...I've made up my mind. Even when I leave Mother\n"
"Base and return to la revolución,\n"
msgstr ""
"……我已经下定决心。即使我离开母基地\n"
"回到革命中，\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/16
msgid ""
"I will never turn to drugs. Nor will I look to the KGB\n"
"for help.\n"
msgstr ""
"我绝不碰毒品。也不向克格勃\n"
"求助。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/17
msgid ""
"If we topple Somoza using the KGB and drug\n"
"money, we will lose the people's hearts.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果我们用克格勃和毒品资金\n"
"推翻索摩查，我们将失去民心。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/18
msgid ""
"So you're choosing a different path from your\n"
"father.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你选了条与你父亲\n"
"不同的路。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/19
msgid ""
"I still respect him. But I will not do things the way\n"
"he did.\n"
msgstr ""
"我仍尊敬他。但不会照\n"
"他的方式行事。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/20
msgid ""
"Well, I'm sure Chico will be glad to hear that.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科听到肯定高兴。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/21
msgid ""
"Chico is a grown soldier now. I could not face him\n"
"otherwise.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科现在是真正战士了。\n"
"不然我没脸见他。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/22
msgid ""
"Well said, Amanda. Those are the words of a true\n"
"comandante.\n"
msgstr ""
"说得好，阿曼达。这是\n"
"真正指挥官的话。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/23
msgid ""
"Stop... I was inspired by the greatest comandante I\n"
"have ever known, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"别……我是受我所见过\n"
"最伟大的指挥官BOSS鼓舞。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, how do I get to the prison camp?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达，怎么去战俘营？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/1
msgid ""
"First head up the narrow mountain path.\n"
msgstr ""
"先沿狭窄的山路上行。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/2
msgid ""
"The path will gradually open up, and you'll come to\n"
"a fork in the road.\n"
msgstr ""
"道路会逐渐开阔，你会来到\n"
"一个岔路口。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/3
msgid ""
"Watch yourself up there.\n"
msgstr ""
"上面小心点。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/4
msgid ""
"You'll be lower than the surrounding terrain,\n"
msgstr ""
"你会处于周围地形之下，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/5
msgid ""
"so if you head down the middle you'll make for an\n"
"easy target.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以走中间，就会成为\n"
"容易的目标。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/6
msgid ""
"Thanks for the heads-up.\n"
msgstr ""
"多谢提醒。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/7
msgid ""
"Take the leftward path to reach the prison camp.\n"
msgstr ""
"走左边的路就能到战俘营。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 431..1030
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/0
msgid ""
"What can you tell me about the prison camp?\n"
msgstr ""
"战俘营的情况怎么样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 1058..2117
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/1
msgid ""
"Well, it used to be a village - until they took control\n"
"of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，这里曾是村庄，直到他们\n"
"控制了它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 2145..3065
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/2
msgid ""
"It is a maze of paths, so watch out for soldiers on\n"
"patrol.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里道路交错，要小心\n"
"巡逻的士兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 3301..3956
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/3
msgid ""
"I'll be sure not to stop and say \"hi.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我肯定不会停下来打招呼。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 3984..4931
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/4
msgid ""
"Use the paths carefully and you should be able to\n"
"stay out of view.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心利用这些道路，你应该能够\n"
"避开视线。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 4959..5489
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/5
msgid ""
"Where are they holding Chico?\n"
msgstr ""
"他们把奇科关在哪？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 5530..6645
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/6
msgid ""
"One of the houses, most likely. You can peek\n"
"through the doors.\n"
msgstr ""
"很可能在某间房里。可从\n"
"门缝偷看。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 6659..7523
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/7
msgid ""
"Just press <I=ACT> when the Icon appears.\n"
msgstr ""
"图标出现时按<I=ACT>。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 7718..8735
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/8
msgid ""
"You could also listen to any sounds inside for clues.\n"
msgstr ""
"也可以听听里面的声音找线索。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 8749..9013
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/9
msgid ""
"Good idea.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 9041..10198
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/10
msgid ""
"Guards will still be on the move while you're looking\n"
"inside. Make sure you don't get caught.\n"
msgstr ""
"你查看里面时，守卫仍在移动。\n"
"确保不要被抓到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 10212..10407
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/11
msgid ""
"And Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 10421..11187
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/12
msgid ""
"I know. I'll bring him back.\n"
msgstr ""
"知道，我带他回来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 11201..12051
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/13
msgid ""
"Thank you. I know I can count on you.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢。我就知道能靠你。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, do you know the way to the rail terminal?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达，去铁路终端怎么走？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/1
msgid ""
"Remember the locomotive? By the fork in the road\n"
"before the village?\n"
msgstr ""
"还记得那辆机车吗？就在村庄前\n"
"的那个岔路口？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, back in the jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，丛林里那台。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/3
msgid ""
"Follow the train tracks from there and you'll come\n"
"to the terminal.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那里沿着铁轨走，你就会到达\n"
"终点站。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/4
msgid ""
"But there's a plant along the way.\n"
msgstr ""
"但路上有个工厂。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/5
msgid ""
"Disguised as a coffee factory?\n"
msgstr ""
"伪装成咖啡厂那个？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/6
msgid ""
"...Yes, it is their drug refining plant. La CIA controls\n"
"it now.\n"
msgstr ""
"……是的，那是他们的毒品提炼厂。现在由中情局控制\n"
"着。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/7
msgid ""
"Cutting through there is the shortest way, but it'll\n"
"be crawling with soldiers.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那里穿过去是最短的路，但那里\n"
"会布满士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/8
msgid ""
"If you want go around...\n"
msgstr ""
"想绕路的话……\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/9
msgid ""
"No, forget it. If that's the shortest way, that's the\n"
"way I'll take.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，算了。如果那是最短的路，那我就走那\n"
"条路。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/10
msgid ""
"Besides, it's one of their bases. It'll be good intel.\n"
msgstr ""
"何况那是他们的基地，能搞到情报。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/11
msgid ""
"Very good. A number of the guards at the plant\n"
"are positioned on high walkways.\n"
msgstr ""
"很好。工厂里的一些守卫\n"
"驻守在高处的走道上。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/12
msgid ""
"Be sure to study their movements before you\n"
"advance.\n"
msgstr ""
"前进前一定要摸清他们的\n"
"行动规律。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/13
msgid ""
"Or I could just snipe them first...\n"
msgstr ""
"或者先狙掉他们……\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/14
msgid ""
"The plant's layout is another maze, I'm afraid. Stay\n"
"cool.\n"
msgstr ""
"恐怕工厂布局又是个迷宫。保持\n"
"冷静。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/15
msgid ""
"Make your way out of the plant and you'll arrive at\n"
"the terminal.\n"
msgstr ""
"从工厂里出去，你就会到达\n"
"终点站。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/16
msgid ""
"You know a lot about this place...\n"
msgstr ""
"你对这地方很熟……\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/17
msgid ""
"What are you saying? I've been there before -\n"
"when the KGB ran it - yes,\n"
msgstr ""
"你说啥？我以前去过那，\n"
"当时克格勃管的，是的，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/18
msgid ""
"but it is not as if I enjoyed it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我可没觉得享受。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/19
msgid ""
"No, I just meant you know a lot about how the\n"
"enemy works.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我只是说你很了解\n"
"敌人的运作方式。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/20
msgid ""
"I hope so.\n"
msgstr ""
"但愿如此。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/21
msgid ""
"Anyway, did you talk to Chico about the terminal?\n"
msgstr ""
"对了，你跟奇科聊过终端吗？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/22
msgid ""
"He said it's where they transfer the cargo onto\n"
"trucks.\n"
msgstr ""
"他说那是把货物转到\n"
"卡车上的地方。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/23
msgid ""
"Meaning the facility is of considerable importance\n"
"to them. Don't get careless.\n"
msgstr ""
"这意味着该设施对他们来说相当重要。\n"
"别大意。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/24
msgid ""
"I won't.\n"
msgstr ""
"不会的。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/25
msgid ""
"By the way,\n"
msgstr ""
"对了，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/26
msgid ""
"I've heard of a shortcut that cuts straight to the\n"
"coffee factory to the east of the village,\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说有条近路能直接通到村子东边的\n"
"咖啡工厂，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/27
msgid ""
"but I've never used it myself. Check it out if you're\n"
"interested.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过我自己没走过。有兴趣的话\n"
"去看看吧。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/28
msgid ""
"Thanks for the tip.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1226
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/0
msgid ""
"An enemy tank! Is there somewhere you can hide,\n"
"Boss?\n"
msgstr ""
"敌方坦克！Boss，有地方躲\n"
"吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 1253..2215
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/1
msgid ""
"There are train cars, but they won't hold up\n"
"against a gun like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"有火车车厢，但它们挡不住\n"
"那样的炮火。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 2243..2869
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/2
msgid ""
"Even a freight train? Incredible!\n"
msgstr ""
"连货运列车都挡不住？厉害！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 3009..3887
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/3
msgid ""
"But they'd keep me out of sight - temporarily.\n"
msgstr ""
"但至少能暂时让我不被发现。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 3914..5196
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/4
msgid ""
"Use them to look for an opportunity to hit its\n"
"treads or the fuel tank at the back, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"利用它们寻找机会攻击它的\n"
"履带或后方的油箱，但是……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 5196..5781
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/5
msgid ""
"Don't forget about that gun, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了那门炮。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 5795..6506
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/6
msgid ""
"Or the soldiers. They may try to flank you.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有士兵。他们可能会包抄你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 6645..8219
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/8
msgid ""
"You can also stop it by taking out all the soldiers.\n"
"You can do it, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"消灭所有士兵也能阻止它。\n"
"你能行，Snake！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1657
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, do I have to take the fork in the road\n"
"back to the village?\n"
msgstr ""
"Amanda，我必须走那个岔路口\n"
"回村庄吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 1685..2925
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/1
msgid ""
"People say there is a shortcut. Go back to the\n"
"coffee factory entrance,\n"
msgstr ""
"人们说有一条捷径。回到\n"
"咖啡工厂入口，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 2939..3469
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/2
msgid ""
"then follow the path on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后走右边的路。\n"
